Generate a C test function for the following execution path.

FUNCTION UNDER TEST:
Name: partition
Signature: int partition(int arr[], int low, int high)
Description: /**
 * @brief Rearranges an array segment around a pivot for quicksort.
 *
 * Partitions the subarray arr[low..high] so that elements less than or equal
 * to the pivot (chosen as arr[high]) are moved before it, and greater elements
 * are moved after. The pivot is placed in its final sorted position.
 *
 * @param arr Array to partition. Must not be NULL.
 * @param low Starting index of the segment (inclusive).
 * @param high Ending index of the segment (inclusive). Must be >= low.
 *
 * @return Index of the pivot after partitioning.
 *
 * @note Modifies arr in-place.
 */
Dependencies: swap

FUNCTION IMPLEMENTATION:
```c
// C program for the function called partition
// Contains target function implementation and dependency signatures

// Forward declarations for dependency functions
void swap(int* a, int* b);

// Target function implementation
int partition (int arr[], int low, int high)
{
    int pivot = arr[high];
    int i = low - 1;

    for (int j = low; j <= high - 1; j++) {
        if (arr[j] <= pivot) {
            i++;
            swap(&arr[i], &arr[j]);
        }
    }
    swap(&arr[i + 1], &arr[high]);
    return i + 1;
}

```

